# Top-level pins for the picture-gen Lambda (Phase 42b), on top of api/requirements.txt. Not installed directly: the
# build installs api/requirements-picture-gen.txt, the hash-pinned lock generated from this file and requirements.txt
# by `python3 scripts/build_lambdas.py --lock picture_gen` (backlog B-4). Change a pin here, regenerate, commit both.
# The bedrock extra brings boto3 and botocore, so the SDK's AWS signing runs on the botocore it was locked with
# (the same version as requirements-dev.txt), not whatever the python3.14 runtime ships.
anthropic[bedrock]==2.8.0
# The OpenAI provider (owner decision 2026-11-16; ADR-0031 "Provider: OpenAI"). 3.48.0 is the newest release published
# at least 7 days before 2026-11-16 (2026-11-09T16:13Z; 3.49.0 to 3.51.0 are newer). No extras: the bedrock extra's
# botocore is not needed (picture-gen reads the key from Secrets Manager with boto3, which is already locked). Its
# dependencies (anyio, httpx2>=2.12, jiter, pydantic, sniffio, typing-extensions) are anthropic's too, so the lock gains
# one wheel.
openai==3.48.0
# Held back from 2.16.2 (published 2026-11-16, the day this lock was made): a dependency release that new is not
# used until it has been out for a while (supply chain).
httpx2==2.16.0
httpcore2==2.16.0
